  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;AIRWAYS INTERNATIONAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Airways International was an airline based in Miami, Florida, operating from 1979 to 1999, with a focus on flights within southern Florida and to the Bahamas, and also operated charter flights. It used various aircraft models including Shorts 330, Convair 580, Cessna 402, Convair 440, and Piper Aztec."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIAMI, FLORIDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Miami, Florida is the base location of Airways International."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANCHORAGE, ALASKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anchorage, Alaska is mentioned as a base location for Airways International in another document, though it does not match the original base location of Miami, Florida."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0037-56a67f50579e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAHAMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bahamas is a destination for Airways International's flights."</data>
